# XCU sh-signals
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XCU.sh-signals.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.12/If job control is disabled
class      required
says       With job control off, a command in an asynchronous list inherits
           SIGINT and SIGQUIT as ignored.
test       t/001-async-ignores-int-quit.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-signals.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.12/commands executed by the shell shall inherit
class      required
says       Other signals keep the action the shell had in an asynchronous
           list: a default-action signal still ends the command.
test       t/002-async-keeps-others.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-signals.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.12/the reception of a signal for which a trap has been set
class      required
says       A signal with a trap that arrives while the shell is in wait
           makes wait return at once with a status above 128, and the trap
           action then runs.
test       t/003-wait-interrupted.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-signals.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.12/shall not be executed until after the foreground command
class      required
says       A trap for a signal that arrives while a foreground utility runs
           is not taken until the utility is done, and the utility is not
           disturbed.
test       t/004-trap-after-foreground.sh
